anchor.text:
Green phoenix plumes are bound into my broom;
At ease I tread Heaven’s gate and sweep the fallen flowers.
See the wind lift clouds of jade-bright dust.
One sudden plunge beneath that bank of cloud:
Beyond the gate, already the ends of earth!
Draw sword no more on Yellow Dragon, going wrong by just a thread;
Nor seek out poor old Dong’s wine-selling home again.
Let you and me lift our eyes towards the glowing clouds.
Dong-bin, when you have found your man, be quick to let me know;
Delay, and you will leave someone grieving among the peach flowers.
